  "title": "# Build: agent-pick (Urgent profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice).",
  "asked": "# Build: agent-pick (Urgent profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice). Assigned agent: **Snap Sully** (book on his card when this starts; if he is still busy and the all-rounder router from crew-retrain #265 is on main, the router may give it to whoever is free - record who in the report). Register in Urgent (id `agent-pick`) + banner entry. ## What Brett wants Every Claude session (voice/chat Amber, Claude Code, headless) runs AS an agent Brett assigns. Claude becomes whichever agent he picks. ## Build on what exists (don't duplicate) - Console **Agent manager** plugin + **Agent swarm** page (agent cards: names, stats, pay $7.50/h, history, write-ups), AmberArt ID card art, crew-live (avatars, AgentAvatar component, agent context menu), follow-amber (console pop-up dialogs + axHub approval stream), claude-settings (Claude plugin, settings on axHub, `claude_settings_get`). Coordinate through their APIs; if one isn't on main yet, build against its contract and note it. ## Steps - s1 **Assign hook:** in Agent manager, every agent row/card has 'Assign to Claude' (and the agent context menu gets it everywhere). Claude settings gets 'Claude agent' = default agent + 'Ask me every session' switch (default ON). - s2 **Agent picker dialog**, opened from the context menu anywhere ('Choose Claude's agent...') and automatically at session start: list of every agent with avatar, name, status (working/idle), current job, today's cost, hours, pay, rating; tap a row to expand ALL details and stats (jobs done, success/fail, average cost and time, recent runs, write-ups, raises) with hooks to their full card, history, Session browser runs, Terminal tabs, group chat. One tap picks. - s3 **Session-start approval:** when a Claude session starts it calls a new MCP tool `claude_session_start` {client: voice|chat|code|headless, summary}. With 'Ask me every session' ON, that pops the picker as a console approval dialog (via follow-amber's pop-up; also an axHub approval item as fallback, and a push to his phone). Until Brett answers, the session uses the default agent. The answer returns {agent id, name, persona/voice notes, avatar}. Headless builds keep their brief's named agent (no prompt) unless Brett turns on 'Ask for headless too'. - s4 **Claude acts as that agent:** the session's work, costs and commits are booked on that agent's card (AXF_AGENT), its avatar shows on everything it does, and it introduces itself by that agent's name. Agent cards get an optional persona/voice field (how they talk) that the session follows. `claude_agent_get` (allow) tells a session who it is. - s5 Rule in shared RULES.md + CLAUDE.md: 'Every Claude session calls claude_session_start first and works as the agent Brett assigns.' Commands declared once -> REST + MCP + CLI. - s6 Zero tokens for the picker/manager code (no LLM imports, test). Tests (ask on/off, default fallback, booking to the right card, picker approval round trip with a fake axHub), phone + desktop screenshots, UI Review item, report `_claude/builds/reports/agent-pick.md`, THREADS, PR, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgr…",
